Subject: [PATCH 1/4] test-writer: emit JSON for non-python cases blocks and
 stop munging code before black

hydrateVariables pasted a cases block's source text for every python target. That is right for a python block and garbage for a javascript one, so grammars.md could not produce a python suite. Paste source only when the block is python and JSON-encode the value otherwise.

formatPython wrapped the code in a triple-quoted string after a hand escape of quotes and backslash-n. The escape turned an escaped newline into a line continuation, so grammars written with "\\n" reached the generated suite with the newline missing. Pass the code as a JSON string literal instead.
